# Test fixture 14 — multiple glasses, different qualifier sets.
#
# Per spec §11.1's resolution: a grammar binds properties PER GLASS,
# not per grammar. This was the load-bearing scoping decision — a
# grammar commonly declares multiple glasses with different target
# ASTs (a grammar with both `to @io` and `to @code/rust` needs
# different qualifier sets because the ASTs differ).
#
# This fixture exercises that resolution: one grammar declares two
# glasses with different qualifier sets. Each glass's qualifier set
# is independent. The same grammar's bodies satisfy DIFFERENT
# constraints depending on which glass they cross.
#
# Expected: parse OK; resolve OK; two glass entries with distinct
#           qualifier sets:
#             to @io          → {halts, io_safety}
#             to @code/rust   → {halts, pure}

in @io
in @code/rust
in @epistemologic/property/halts
in @epistemologic/property/io_safety
in @epistemologic/property/pure

grammar @test/14/multi_glass {
  # Each glass binds the qualifier set appropriate to its target AST.
  # `halts` is universal (every body must terminate). `io_safety`
  # makes sense at @io (where the @io discipline applies). `pure`
  # makes sense at @code/rust (where the Rust AST can be walked for
  # purity).
  glass to @io {
    property halts
    property io_safety
  }

  glass to @code/rust {
    property halts
    property pure
  }
}
